ntent":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The cost properties are optional on purpose: they arrive flat, and a field that does not apply","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the named function is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"absent, not zero"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". Reading a missing ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/memoryKib","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stretch at the wrong cost and fail against a record that is perfectly good (§23.4 rule 5).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These are never cached across exchanges and never defaulted locally. A credential enrolled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under one cost keeps working after a tenant raises its policy, so a client that guessed would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derive a different randomized password and report “invalid password” for one that is entirely"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"correct (§23.4 rule 2)."}]},{"anchor":"This-is-where-Swift-stopped-needing-a-pbkdf2sha256-tenant","type":"heading","text":"This is where Swift stopped needing a `pbkdf2_sha256` tenant","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SRP client this replaces refused an "},{"code":"argon2id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tenant outright: Swift has no Argon2 that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ships on every supported platform, and substituting PBKDF2 would have derived a different "},{"code":"x","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and surfaced as “invalid password”. AXIAM’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"